{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"Noah","id":"360967589511561218","is_bot":0,"username":"king.crusader"},"author_id":"360967589511561218","channel_id":"851694513068179477","content":"Finn repeats the knowledge he wrote down out loud\n\n```A miracle of the Modern Age. The Empire City Clocktower is said to have been commissioned and built overnight. Now, a symbol of the city in it's own right, it is best know for it's security system, a seemingly endless series of traps and treasure. However, it has often been reported but never confirmed,  that dwarven residents dressed as Elk's lodge acolytes and elves adorned as members of the  Oddfellows masquerade can sometimes been seen entering the building at the same time. Some suggest that this is a formal dance or celebration of the oldest families if Empire City.\"\n\n\n\"The doors open at seemingly random times, and the most viscous traps await those who enter, but vast sums of wealth have been found within. Some speculate that it might be a test of some kind. Others that it is an elaborate security system designed to kill or buy off those searching it to prevent all but the most dedicated from finding the end.```","created_at":"2021-08-25T04:25:16.602000Z","edited_at":"2021-08-25T04:25:24.358000Z","id":"879944496744366130","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
